=== two genuine test-writing bugs found and fixed before sealing ===
test_the_proposer_own_signature_is_never_counted_even_if_otherwise_valid and
test_an_unresolved_signatory_is_never_counted originally used only 2
signatures each, so excluding the proposer/unresolved one left only 1
distinct valid signatory when 2 are required -- QUORUM_NOT_MET fires
before MISSING_REQUIRED_ROLE is ever reached, correct implementation
behavior the tests' own expectations had not accounted for. Fixed by
adding a third, genuinely distinct and valid signatory so quorum (2)
stays satisfiable on its own, isolating the intended proposer-exclusion/
unresolved-identity behavior: the failure is role coverage, not raw
headcount.

